.. raw:: html

    <div class="sphx-glr-thumbcontainer" tooltip="In 1946, Lev Landau solved the linearized Vlasov equation for a wave on a Maxwellian plasma and found something that seemed to violate reversible mechanics: the wave damps, exponentially, with no collisions or dissipation anywhere in the equations. Particles moving at very nearly the wave&#x27;s phase velocity &quot;surf&quot; it, and because a thermal distribution always has slightly more slightly slower particles being accelerated than slightly faster particles being decelerated, the net exchange drains the wave.">

.. only:: html

  .. image:: /api/gallery/plasma/kinetic/images/thumb/sphx_glr_plot_01_landau_damping_thumb.png
